::SQL DEFAULT::
Which of the following is not accurate?
{
    ~The DEFAULT constraint is used to set a default value for a column.
    ~The DEFAULT value will be added to all new records if no other value is specified.
    =The DEFAULT value must be unique for every column of every record.
    ~DEFAULT values are typically literal constants, although many database systems allow timestamp or datetime columns to use functions such as CURRENT_TIMESTAMP.
}

::SQL DEFAULT::
You can use the DEFAULT constraint to pre-fill a timestamp for a record that is being inserted.
{
    =True
    ~False
}
